<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">Result</p>
    <p class="lede">Between zero and one, a symmetric endpoint measure totals π. Open that interval into
      its affine diameter and the same integral is the length of a unit semicircle. The theorem is exact;
      the cosmological reading is a proposal.</p>
    <p>The corrected TTI chain therefore reads: zero and one provide the normalised boundaries; Euclidean
      closure supplies the circular metric; integration measures the return; π is the constant that makes
      those statements agree.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Return to <a href="/foundations/#t-pi">π as the condition of closure</a>, or
      continue to <a href="/the-self/">Part I &mdash; First Principles: The Self</a>.</p>
